  "behavior": [
    "Remove Rprintf String::from_utf8_unchecked. Snapshot the exact native C bytes into a forbidunsafe owned byte buffer and validate that the supplied admission equals the actual byte length.",
    "Acquire original runtime pin and reserve complete workspace through the existing callback-free metadata path before copying. Registered arena lends use their actual ledger without reborrowing the arena or entering R; own the snapshot before any formatter/TLS buffer could be changed by a native callout.",
    "Use a typed original OwnerToken for the byte-output entry, pin it through native writes and recheck authority on normal return and callback unwind. Source bytes and their ticket outlive the complete write, with Vec storage dropped before its guard.",
    "One byte route forwards unchanged bytes to existing native sinks and connections. Only String capture frames convert invalid byte units to ASCII hex escapes, retaining valid Unicode spans and all original stream ordering/split behavior.",
    "Stream capture conversion without allocating a complete rendered message. Each receiving frame applies its existing byte cap at UTF8 boundaries, and chronological mirrors copy only its admitted text prefix. Raising a later cap can accept new text even when the old truncation flag is already true.",
    "Output outside an interpreter continues to native stdout as bytes. Existing printf variadic/format-only contract is unchanged."
  ],
